<section id="encrypted-sharing" aria-labelledby="sharing-mechanics-heading" class="content-defer bg-slate-900 py-16 sm:py-24 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-emerald-400">04 • Share a Link to an Item</p>
            <h2 id="sharing-mechanics-heading" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
                How URL Fragment (#) Sharing Keeps Decryption Keys Off the Server
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
                When you click <strong>Share</strong> on any item, PassKee clones the credential, strips any file attachments on your device, encrypts the payload with a fresh 256-bit AES-GCM key, and appends the 64-character hex key after <code class="rounded bg-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-emerald-300">#</code>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-10 rounded-3xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-950 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-2xl">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
                <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400">Exact Format of a PassKee Share Link</p>
                <span class="rounded-full border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/10 px-3 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-amber-300">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>Files attached to an item are never shared
                </span>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-4 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm break-all leading-relaxed">
                <span class="text-blue-400">https://passkee.org/share/0195f8a27c4b7d3e9a10</span><span class="rounded bg-emerald-500/20 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-500/30">#8f9d2a7e4c1b09f36d5a8e2c1b4f7a90e3c6d1b8f4a209c7e5d3b1a8f6c4e290</span>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
                <div class="rounded-2xl border border-blue-500/30 bg-blue-950/20 p-5">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-300">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-server" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span>Sent to PassKee Server (Before #)</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-blue-200">/share/0195f8a27c4b7d3e9a10</p>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
                        Fetches the AES-256-GCM ciphertext blob and enforces your chosen expiration (<strong class="text-white">1 hour, 1 day, 7 days, or 30 days</strong>) and view limit (<strong class="text-white">Can be viewed only once</strong>).
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-950/20 p-5">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-300">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span>Stays Strictly in Recipient's Browser (After #)</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-emerald-200">#8f9d2a7e4c1b09f3... (256-bit Hex Key)</p>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
                        By HTTP specification, browsers never send the <code class="font-mono">#</code> fragment over the network. The recipient's browser extracts the hex key locally to decrypt the shared item in memory.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

